"help.title" = "How to use Blinds";
"help.text" = "1. Hold ⌘ and drag the menu bar icons you want to hide to the left of the │ dividers.\n2. Click the arrow to hide or show them. Keyboard: ⌃⌥⌘B.\n3. Right-click the arrow for options.\n\nIf the menu bar is full, icons that don't fit stay hidden by macOS even when Blinds is open (on macOS 27 you find them in its « menu).\n\nIf the arrow disappears: press ⌃⌥⌘B, or open Blinds again from Spotlight.";
"alert.newDividers.title" = "Move the new dividers next to the arrow";
"alert.newDividers.text" = "To hide icons on wide screens too, Blinds now uses several │ dividers side by side. The new ones appeared at the far left of the menu bar.\n\nHold ⌘ and drag each new │ until it sits next to the │ beside the arrow. You only do this once: macOS remembers where they go.\n\nIcons to the left of all the dividers get hidden.";
